  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Intermon</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">On 8 September 2023 a powerful earthquake of magnitude 6.8 struck Morocco at 18.5 km depth. The epicenter was in the High Atlas Mountains, 71km (44 miles) south-west of Marrakesh. Marrakesh, with a population of 840,000 inhabitants is the most impacted city. According to media, several houses have collapsed and other buildings were reported with structural damage. The epicentral area is not densely populated. According to the national authorities, 2,946 people died while the amount of injured people reached 5,674.
Initialassessments indicate that WASH, shelter, health, and food assistance are required. Several aftershocks have been reported.  Oxfam Novib launched a public appeal to support the earthquake-affected families.</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org role="4" type="24">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Intermon Oxfam Maroc</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Intermon Oxfam has been working in Morocco since 1993, and it has been working with local organisations in longer-term partnerships. During the coming five years, Intermon Oxfam in Morocco will implement three main programs which correlate with Oxfam Novib&apos;s strategies for the country:
- A program on womens rights, focusing on combating violence against women, increase participation of women in decision-making and fostering a culture of female citizenship and equality;
- An Economic Justice program, including income-generating activities, labour rights and corporate social responsibility, as well as trade agreements;
- A citizenship and governance program supporting the rule of law, justice reform and constitutional reform; supporting civil society networks and forums; as well as budget monitoring and accountability in public affairs.</narrative>
  </participating-org>
